    {
      "id": 417,
      "title": "Prediction accuracy, drift and feature health",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 27,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**ACCURACY_NOT_AVAILABLE.** Production accuracy needs a prediction paired with the outcome that later occurred. This platform captures that only for shadow predictions, and no model is serving in production, so there is no production accuracy to plot. A panel showing 100%, 0% or a training score relabelled as accuracy would each be a fabrication.\n\n**DRIFT \u2014 MEASUREMENT_ONLY.** Freshness and horizon expiry are measured above and are the drift signals this platform can currently support. Distribution drift (PSI / KL) has no defined threshold here, so it is not alerted: `ALERT_POLICY_UNSET`.\n\n**FEATURE HEALTH \u2014 partial.** Feature availability is measured through the readiness assessment (`/api/admin/ml/readiness`), which counts rows, missingness and leakage per model. It is a point-in-time API result rather than a time series, so it is not charted here; the runbook says where to read it."
      }
    }
  ]
